.TH "C3L" "1" "2026-11-12"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
\fBc3l\fR - reproducible dependencies for C3 projects: from registries, git or a local directory.\&
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBc3l\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
\fBc3l\fR \fB--version\fR | \fB--help\fR | \fBhelp\fR [\fICOMMAND\fR]
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBc3l\fR installs the libraries a project needs and records each one, with its version and
the SHA-256 of what it installed, in a lockfile, \fIc3l.\&lock\fR.\& A download that does not match
its checksum is refused, a failed update rolls back, and \fBupdate\fR, \fBoutdated\fR, \fBremove\fR and
\fBsync\fR work from the lockfile.\& Libraries are kept as \fI.\&c3l\fR zip files in the first entry of
\fIdependency-search-paths\fR (\fIlib\fR is added if there is none); commit them, or ignore them and
run \fBc3l sync\fR after cloning.\& Run \fBc3l\fR in the project root.\&
.PP
c3l fetches from any registry that serves \fIinfo/<ns>/<name>\fR and the downloads, and from c3pkg.\&
A library in the library directory that \fIc3l.\&lock\fR does not list is shown as \fIuntracked\fR and
fails \fBverify\fR and \fBsync --frozen\fR until it is added with \fBc3l add\fR.\& Registries that need a
login to download are not supported.\&
.PP
\fBadd\fR and \fBupdate\fR list each registry library in \fIproject.\&json\fR with its full path,
\fI[url:]ns/name@version:sha256\fR (see \fBDEPENDENCIES\fR).\& \fBsync\fR restores every library from
\fIc3l.\&lock\fR at the locked version and checksum.\&
.PP
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.PP
\fBc3l\fR is linked against \fBlibcurl\fR.\& At run time it needs \fBc3c\fR 0.\&8.\&6 or newer (it reads the
project with \fBc3c project view\fR, and runs \fBinit\fR, the compile checks of \fBcheck\fR and the
build of a \fIsource-lib\fR target through it) and \fBgit\fR (git libraries and submodules, and
\fBcheck\fR, \fBpack\fR, \fBpublish\fR in a git repository).\& It talks to registries itself; registry
libraries need no \fBgit\fR.\& With a \fBc3c\fR older than 0.\&8.\&6, \fBadd\fR, \fBupdate\fR and \fBsync\fR warn
that an updated \fI.\&c3l\fR archive may keep compiling its old sources.\&
.PP
On Windows, \fBgit\fR is Git for Windows, and linking a local directory (\fBadd\fR \fI.\&/dir\fR)
needs Developer Mode or an administrator, for whom Windows creates symbolic links.\&
Git for Windows checks files out with CRLF line endings by default
(\fIcore.\&autocrlf=true\fR), so a package packed there differs from one packed on
Linux; a library that wants the same bytes everywhere sets \fI* text=auto eol=lf\fR
in its \fI.\&gitattributes\fR.\& c3l reads a \fIc3l.\&lock\fR with either line ending.\&
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
The options from \fB--registry\fR to \fB--registry-type\fR may appear before or after the
command.\& The publishing options, from \fB--version\fR to \fB--target\fR, follow \fBcheck\fR,
\fBpack\fR or \fBpublish\fR.\&
.PP
\fB--registry\fR \fINAME|URL\fR, \fB--registry=\fR\fINAME|URL\fR
.RS 4
The registry for \fBadd\fR, \fBsearch\fR, \fBinfo\fR and \fBpublish\fR: a base URL (path included) or the name of a default, \fIc3pkg\fR or \fIc3lang\fR.\& \fBsearch\fR and
\fBinfo\fR use all of them (repeat it); \fBadd\fR takes the first, and warns if there are more; \fBpublish\fR takes one.\& Without it c3l uses
the defaults (see \fBREGISTRIES\fR).\& \fBC3L_REGISTRY\fR is the same, comma separated.\&
Libraries already in \fIc3l.\&lock\fR are always fetched from the registry recorded for them.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--dry-run\fR
.RS 4
Only print what \fBupdate\fR or \fBprune\fR would change, or stop \fBpublish\fR before the
upload.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--frozen\fR
.RS 4
For \fBsync\fR, meant for CI.\& Fail if \fIproject.\&json\fR and \fIc3l.\&lock\fR list different
libraries, restore only what the lockfile says, and never write the lockfile.\&
Has no effect on other commands.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--strict\fR
.RS 4
With \fBadd\fR and \fBupdate\fR: fail instead of warn when the registry says a library
was published for another C3 release than your \fBc3c\fR (compared by
major.\&minor), or does not list your platform, and when libraries require each
other in a cycle or a library requires itself.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--fail-fast\fR
.RS 4
With \fBsync\fR and \fBupdate\fR: stop at the first library that fails.\& The default is to
go on with the others and report the failures at the end (exit status 1).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--force\fR
.RS 4
With \fBremove\fR: remove the library even if another library requires it.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--allow-host\fR \fIHOST\fR
.RS 4
Trust \fIHOST\fR for git or registry dependencies named by a library'\&s \fIc3l.\&lock\fR or
\fImanifest.\&json\fR.\& Local paths and \fBfile://\fR URLs are the host \fIfile\fR.\& Can be
repeated.\& See \fBDEPENDENCIES\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--registry-type\fR \fIstatic|c3pkg\fR
.RS 4
Override the detected registry type.\& See \fBPUBLISHING\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--version\fR \fIX.\&Y.\&Z\fR, \fB--version=\fR\fIX.\&Y.\&Z\fR
.RS 4
After \fBcheck\fR, \fBpack\fR or \fBpublish\fR: the version to publish.\& Before any command,
\fB--version\fR prints the version of \fBc3l\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--token-file\fR \fIFILE\fR
.RS 4
File with the registry API token (first line).\& See \fBPUBLISHING\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--description\fR \fITEXT\fR, \fB--license\fR \fIID\fR, \fB--tags\fR \fIa,b\fR, \fB--docs-url\fR \fIURL\fR, \fB--git-url\fR \fIURL\fR
.RS 4
Package metadata for \fBpublish\fR.\& The description is required the first time a
package is published.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--c3-version\fR \fIX.\&Y.\&Z\fR
.RS 4
C3 version sent to the registry.\& Default: the version of \fBc3c\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--output\fR \fIFILE\fR
.RS 4
For \fBpack\fR: where to write the package.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--list\fR
.RS 4
For \fBcheck\fR and \fBpack\fR: print each file of the package with the rule that took it
(\fImanifest\fR, \fIsource pattern\fR \fIP\fR, \fIheader\fR, \fIplatform library\fR \fID\fR, \fIexec\fR, \fIlicence\fR,
\fIreadme\fR, \fIlock\fR), then the tracked files left out.\& \fBpack --list\fR writes no package.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--target\fR \fINAME\fR
.RS 4
For \fBcheck\fR, \fBpack\fR and \fBpublish\fR of a project that has no \fImanifest.\&json\fR and several
\fIsource-lib\fR targets: the one to pack.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--allow-dirty\fR
.RS 4
Let \fBcheck\fR, \fBpack\fR and \fBpublish\fR run on a working tree with uncommitted changes.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--no-build\fR
.RS 4
Skip the compile check in \fBcheck\fR, \fBpack\fR and \fBpublish\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--offline\fR
.RS 4
Do not query the registry in \fBcheck\fR (the registry is always skipped by \fBpack\fR).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--tree\fR
.RS 4
After \fBlist\fR: print the dependency graph instead of the table.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB-h\fR, \fB--help\fR
.RS 4
Print the usage text, of \fBc3l\fR or of the command it follows.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH COMMANDS
.PP
Some commands have short names: \fBadd\fR is also \fBfetch\fR, \fBf\fR, \fBget\fR and \fBg\fR; \fBremove\fR is
\fBrm\fR, \fBr\fR and \fBdelete\fR; \fBupdate\fR is \fBu\fR; \fBsync\fR is \fBpull\fR and \fBp\fR; \fBlist\fR is \fBls\fR and \fBl\fR;
\fBsearch\fR is \fBs\fR.\&
.PP
\fBinit\fR [\fIname\fR]
.RS 4
Create \fIc3l.\&lock\fR.\& With \fIname\fR and outside a project, run \fBc3c init\fR first.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBadd\fR \fInamespace/name\fR[@\fIversion\fR]
.RS 4
Install a library from the registry, compare the SHA-256 of the download with
the registry'\&s checksum, write the lock line.\& The version can also be given as a
separate argument.\& A mismatch or any failure restores the previous library file
and \fIproject.\&json\fR.\& The library is listed in \fIproject.\&json\fR with its full path
(see \fBDEPENDENCIES\fR).\&
.PP
.RE
\fBadd\fR [\fIurl\fR:]\fInamespace/name\fR[@\fIversion\fR][:\fIsha256\fR]
.RS 4
The same in the full path form, as it appears in \fIdependencies\fR: the registry url
(else \fB--registry\fR or the default), the version and the SHA-256 of the download are each
optional.\& A checksum needs a version, and must match what the registry serves.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBadd\fR \fI.\&/dir\fR
.RS 4
Link a local library directory (\fI.\&/dir\fR, \fI.\&.\&/dir\fR or an absolute path with a
\fImanifest.\&json\fR) into \fIlib/\fR with a relative symlink, so edits show up in the next
build and the project and the directory can move together.\& \fBverify\fR checks where
the link points.\&
Recorded in the lockfile as kind \fIpath\fR; \fBsync\fR re-creates the link, \fBupdate\fR skips
it, and its own dependencies are followed.\& A library that depends on a local
directory cannot be published.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBadd\fR \fIgit-url\fR[@\fIref\fR]
.RS 4
Install from a git repository.\& \fIgithub.\&com/owner/repo\fR and \fIcodeberg.\&org/owner/repo\fR
without a scheme mean their https URL; for ssh, give the ssh URL
(\fIgit@github.\&com:owner/repo\fR).\& \fIref\fR is a tag, a branch, \fBHEAD\fR, or a full
40-character commit hash; it can also be given as a separate argument.\& Without
a \fIref\fR the highest release tag is used (prerelease tags such as \fIv1.\&0.\&0-rc.\&1\fR only
when asked for), or HEAD if there are none.\& The ref is resolved to a commit,
which is what the lockfile pins.\& \fBoutdated\fR and \fBupdate\fR move a tag to the
highest release tag and follow the tip of \fBHEAD\fR and of branches; commits stay
put; a tag only moves to a compatible version (see \fBDEPENDENCIES\fR).\& In scp-style URLs (\fIgit@host:path\fR) the \fB@\fR only starts a ref after the
last \fB/\fR.\& URLs with credentials (\fIhttps://user:token@host/.\&.\&.\&\fR) are refused: the
URL is written to the lockfile; see \fBPRIVATE REPOSITORIES\fR.\& The library is built with \fBgit archive\fR, so no \fI.\&git\fR is included, and without
line-ending conversion.\& A git library is identified by its commit and its files:
the lockfile pins the commit and records a hash of the files in the archive, and
\fBverify\fR and \fBsync\fR check both (\fBgit archive\fR stores the commit id in the zip
comment).\& The hash covers names and contents only, so it does not depend on the
git version that built the archive.\& This needs \fBgit\fR.\& The repository needs a \fImanifest.\&json\fR at its root.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBremove\fR \fIname\fR
.RS 4
Delete the library file, its \fIdependencies\fR entry and its lock line.\& Refuses if
another library requires it (\fB--force\fR overrides) and lists libraries that are no
longer needed.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBprune\fR
.RS 4
Remove dependency libraries that no directly added library needs any more.\&
With \fB--dry-run\fR only list them.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBwhy\fR \fIname\fR
.RS 4
Show which libraries require \fIname\fR, and why they are installed.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBlist\fR [\fB--tree\fR]
.RS 4
Show every locked library with its state: \fIok\fR, \fImodified\fR, \fImissing\fR,
\fIunpacked\fR, and \fIuntracked\fR for libraries in \fIproject.\&json\fR not in the lockfile.\&
\fIdep\fR marks a library pulled in by another one, \fIsubmodule\fR one stored as a git
submodule (with its own states, see \fBGIT SUBMODULES\fR).\& With \fB--tree\fR print the
dependency graph.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBverify\fR
.RS 4
Check installed files against the lockfile.\& Exit status 1 on any difference.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBoutdated\fR
.RS 4
Show locked libraries for which the registry (or git) has a higher version: the
newest compatible version, which \fBupdate\fR moves to, and a newer version that
is not compatible, if there is one (see \fBDEPENDENCIES\fR).\& A library whose source cannot be reached is named, and
the exit status is 1.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBupdate\fR [\fIname\fR[@\fIref\fR] .\&.\&.\&]
.RS 4
Update to the newest compatible version, one library at a time, with
rollback; a newer version that is not compatible is only announced.\& With \fIname\fR@\fIref\fR switch
that library to an explicit version instead: a registry version, or for git
libraries a tag, branch, \fBHEAD\fR or full commit hash (for example \fBc3l update
lib@HEAD\fR moves a tag-locked library to HEAD).\& Moving to a version that is not
compatible fails if a library that requires it asks for the old one.\& A name that is not in
the lockfile is an error.\& With \fB--dry-run\fR only print what would change.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBsync\fR
.RS 4
Make the project match \fIc3l.\&lock\fR: reinstall missing or modified libraries at the
locked version and verify against the locked checksum or commit.\& With
\fB--frozen\fR fail instead if \fIproject.\&json\fR and the lockfile list different
libraries, and never write the lockfile.\& A plain name in \fIproject.\&json\fR for a locked registry
library is accepted by \fB--frozen\fR (older projects), but a full path must match the lock:
name, version, checksum and registry.\& Without \fB--frozen\fR, \fBsync\fR (like \fBupdate\fR) writes the
full path in place of a plain name.\& A library that cannot be restored does
not stop the others: \fBsync\fR goes on, then exits with status 1 and names the
failures.\& \fB--fail-fast\fR stops at the first one.\& Each library is still restored
atomically.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBsearch\fR \fItext\fR | \fBtag:\fR\fIname\fR
.RS 4
Search the registries, all at once (one thread each, 10 seconds to answer), by name and
description.\& Each hit shows its registry, in the order of the registries; one that does
not answer is a warning.\& A static registry has no search API: c3l reads its \fIindex.\&json\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBinfo\fR \fInamespace/name\fR
.RS 4
Show the registry record of a library: its versions and their checksums, and
whether the latest one suits this C3 release and platform.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBversion\fR
.RS 4
Print the version.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBhelp\fR [\fIcommand\fR]
.RS 4
Print the usage text of \fBc3l\fR or of \fIcommand\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBcompletion\fR \fIbash\fR|\fIzsh\fR|\fIfish\fR
.RS 4
Print a shell completion script.\& See \fBSHELL COMPLETION\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBmigrate\fR
.RS 4
Convert a c3po \fIproject.\&lock.\&json\fR, or the \fI.\&c3l.\&deps\fR of c3l 0.\&x, into
\fIc3l.\&lock\fR.\& The libraries are locked as git libraries: c3po'\&s commits, or the
commit each 0.\&x tag points to now.\& The old file is not touched; run \fBsync\fR
afterwards to rebuild the libraries as verified archives.\& Also adopts git
submodules in the library directory that the lockfile does not list yet, into a
new or an existing \fIc3l.\&lock\fR (see \fBGIT SUBMODULES\fR).\&
.PP
.RE
\fBcheck\fR [\fIdir\fR]
.RS 4
Verify that the library in \fIdir\fR (default: .\&) can be published, without
uploading: \fImanifest.\&json\fR with \fIprovides\fR (or a \fIsource-lib\fR target, see \fBpack\fR), a valid
version, a clean working tree, the files the manifest names exist, and the package
compiles: the staged package is compiled for this platform with only the libraries its
\fIc3l.\&lock\fR brings, then without object files for each other platform in the manifest'\&s
\fItargets\fR (a platform a dependency does not support, or that needs the Android NDK, is
skipped with a note).\& The version must not be on the registry yet.\& A library in \fIlib/\fR
that the manifest depends on but \fIc3l.\&lock\fR does not list is an error (see \fBPUBLISHING\fR).\&
Warnings: a package that holds test code (\fI*\fRtest.\&c3_ or an \fI@test\fR function), which
consumers compile too, and a manifest pattern that matches no file.\& Exit status 1 on any
problem.\& \fB--list\fR prints the package contents.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBpack\fR [\fIdir\fR]
.RS 4
Write \fIname-version.\&c3l\fR (or \fB--output\fR): a zip of what the library needs, \fIc3l.\&lock\fR
included (when it has entries).\& The archive is deterministic, the same tree gives the
same bytes.\& The files come from those git tracks or does not ignore (all files without
git; never \fI.\&git\fR, \fIlib/\fR, \fIobj/\fR or \fIbuild/\fR), selected as the compiler reads a library:
\fImanifest.\&json\fR; the C3 sources (\fI.\&c3\fR, \fI.\&c3i\fR, \fI.\&c3t\fR) of \fIsources\fR and of each target'\&s
\fIsources\fR and \fIsources-override\fR (a file, a directory and \fIdir/**\fR with everything below,
\fIdir/*\fR the files in it; without \fIsources\fR the top directory, not recursive); the C files
(\fI.\&c\fR, \fI.\&m\fR) of \fIc-sources\fR and the target forms, with the headers (\fI.\&h\fR, \fI.\&hh\fR, \fI.\&hpp\fR,
\fI.\&hxx\fR, \fI.\&inc\fR) next to them and in \fIc-include-dirs\fR; the files below \fIlinklib-dir\fR (else the
library) \fI/<os-arch>/\fR for each platform in \fItargets\fR (any platform without \fItargets\fR), or
\fI/<os>/\fR when there is no such directory; the files a command of \fIexec\fR names (c3l cannot
see what else a script uses, and warns); \fILICENSE*\fR and \fIREADME*\fR of the top directory.\& A
pattern that matches only ignored files, or that leaves the library (\fI.\&.\&\fR, an absolute
path), is an error.\& A project with a \fIsource-lib\fR target and no \fImanifest.\&json\fR is packed
from what \fBc3c build\fR writes for the target in a temporary directory (the project'\&s own
\fIbuild/\fR is not touched), plus \fIc3l.\&lock\fR; \fB--target\fR picks one of several targets.\& Package
dependencies are plain library names, never full paths.\& \fB--list\fR shows the rule for each
file and the files left out, and writes nothing.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBpublish\fR [\fIdir\fR]
.RS 4
Run \fBcheck\fR, \fBpack\fR and upload to the registry, then compare the registry'\&s
checksum with the uploaded file.\& With \fB--dry-run\fR stop before the upload.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH REGISTRIES
.PP
c3l knows two registries: \fIc3pkg\fR (www.\&c3pkg.\&eu) and \fIc3lang\fR (the vendor collection:
sqlite3, raylib, curl and the like, as \fIc3lang/<name>\fR).\& The list will grow.\& \fBsearch\fR and \fBinfo\fR
ask all of them.\& \fBadd\fR \fIns/name\fR asks none: it fetches from \fIc3pkg\fR, or from \fIc3lang\fR when the
namespace is \fIc3lang\fR, or from the registry given with \fB--registry\fR (the first, if several are set, with a warning).\& To find out where a library
is, \fBsearch\fR it.\& A dependency that names no registry follows the same rule.\& The registry a
library was installed from is in \fIc3l.\&lock\fR; \fBsync\fR, \fBupdate\fR, \fBoutdated\fR and \fBverify\fR go
there and ask nobody else.\&
.PP
c3l 2.\&1 and older locked the vendor collection as \fIvendor\fR entries.\& \fBmigrate\fR turns them into
\fIc3lang\fR entries; \fBsync\fR then installs them from the registry (the archives differ).\&
.PP
.SH PUBLISHING
.PP
\fBpublish\fR needs a registry with an upload API.\& Registry types: \fIc3pkg\fR (www.\&c3pkg.\&eu;
detected by probing \fI/api/v1/packages\fR) and \fIstatic\fR (read-only, anything else).\&
.PP
A \fIstatic\fR registry is a tree of files: \fIinfo/<ns>/<name>\fR lists the versions with
their checksum, and each version is downloaded from its own \fIurl\fR when the record has one
(the \fIc3lang/vendor\fR registry points at release assets), else from \fIdownload/<ns>/<name>@<version>\fR.\&
A version that c3pkg marks yanked still installs for whoever locked it, with a warning.\&
.PP
For c3pkg: create an API token under Settings, API tokens, and give it to c3l with
\fB--token-file\fR \fIFILE\fR, \fBC3L_TOKEN\fR or \fBC3PKG_TOKEN\fR.\& It is sent as
\fIAuthorization: Bearer\fR header and never appears on a command line.\&
.PP
The package name is \fIprovides\fR in \fImanifest.\&json\fR of the library directory (see
\fBc3c init-lib\fR), or the name of the \fIsource-lib\fR target of a project without one.\& The version is, in this order: \fB--version\fR, a semantic version tag on
HEAD (\fIv1.\&2.\&3\fR or \fI1.\&2.\&3\fR), \fIversion\fR in \fImanifest.\&json\fR, \fIversion\fR in
\fIproject.\&json\fR (\fImanifest.\&json\fR wins).\& If the manifest or the project file says
something else, c3l warns and the archive gets the chosen version; the files in the
repository are not changed.\& A version is \fIMAJOR.\&MINOR.\&PATCH\fR or
\fIMAJOR.\&MINOR.\&PATCH-prerelease\fR and can never be changed once published.\&
.PP
A package carries no other library: c3c finds a library only next to the others in
the project'\&s library directory, never inside one.\& Dependencies travel in
\fIc3l.\&lock\fR instead, and installers fetch them; a library in \fIlib/\fR that is not in
\fIc3l.\&lock\fR stays behind, so \fBcheck\fR refuses one the manifest depends on.\& Either
publish it (registry or git) and \fBc3l add\fR it, or vendor its sources: put them in
the library (e.\&g.\& \fIvendor/name/\fR) and list them in \fI"sources"\fR, so they are
compiled as part of it (rename the module, e.\&g.\& \fImylib::name\fR, to avoid a clash
with the real library).\&
.PP
The C3 version of the library is sent with each upload and checked on \fBadd\fR and
\fBinfo\fR: a different major.\&minor or a missing platform gives a warning (an error
with \fB--strict\fR).\&
.PP
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.PP
A library directory (a \fImanifest.\&json\fR and no \fIproject.\&json\fR) works too: \fBadd\fR installs
into \fI.\&/lib\fR (keep it out of git; it is never packed), lists only the dependencies you
asked for in the manifest'\&s \fIdependencies\fR, and writes \fIc3l.\&lock\fR.\& Commit the lock: it is
how the library declares its dependencies, and it travels with the library, in its git
archive and in the package \fBpack\fR builds.\&
.PP
A library'\&s dependencies are not installed transitively by the project: every one must
be in \fIproject.\&json\fR.\& \fBadd\fR and \fBupdate\fR therefore follow the dependencies a library
declares and add them all, flat, to \fIlib\fR and \fIproject.\&json\fR, as one transaction.\&
.PP
In \fIproject.\&json\fR, \fBadd\fR and \fBupdate\fR list a registry library with its full path,
\fI[url:]ns/name@version:sha256\fR, the exact version and archive checksum of \fIc3l.\&lock\fR; the
registry url is left out for \fIc3lang\fR.\& Anyone can then restore these libraries with
\fBc3c project fetch\fR instead of \fBc3l sync\fR.\& A plain name or an older path of the same
library is replaced; \fBremove\fR and \fBprune\fR drop the entry in either form; comments and
layout of the file stay as they are.\& Git and local libraries are listed by name, and a
library'\&s \fImanifest.\&json\fR and the package \fBpack\fR builds never get a full path.\& With
\fBsync --frozen\fR a full path that disagrees with \fIc3l.\&lock\fR fails and a plain name still
passes; plain \fBsync\fR and \fBupdate\fR upgrade it to the full path.\&
.PP
A library declares them in its \fIc3l.\&lock\fR: each direct entry is a requirement, from
the source it names (a registry the consumer has no library from yet needs
\fB--allow-host\fR), at least at the locked version for registry libraries, at the locked
tag, branch or commit for git libraries (\fBupdate\fR moves a tag like any other version).\&
Apps and libraries alike, \fIc3l.\&lock\fR is the only file c3l writes dependencies to.\& So a library that was never
touched by c3l but lists its dependencies as paths still installs them all, and they
end up in \fIc3l.\&lock\fR as dependencies; c3l never writes a path into a manifest.\& c3pkg
refuses paths in \fIdependencies\fR, and \fBcheck\fR says so before you upload.\&
.PP
c3l also reads, but never writes, \fIvendor.\&c3l.\&requires\fR in a library'\&s \fImanifest.\&json\fR
(packages published by c3l 1.\&1), c3po'\&s \fIvendor.\&c3po.\&sources\fR (\fIc3po-version\fR 1; at
the commit the library'\&s \fIproject.\&lock.\&json\fR pins, if it has one) and
c3c'\&s \fIdependencies\fR: a plain name (no source: a warning, and \fBverify\fR fails until the
library is added) or a library path, \fI[url:]ns/name[@version][:sha256]\fR, which names
the source (\fIns/name\fR in the registry at \fIurl\fR, else the default), the minimum version
and the checksum that version'\&s archive must have (64 hex digits, needs a version; a
mismatch with the file or the registry is an error).\& c3c accepts a path wherever it takes a
name and reduces it to the name itself.\& For each name the first wins, in this order: \fIvendor.\&c3l.\&requires\fR,
\fIc3l.\&lock\fR, \fIvendor.\&c3po.\&sources\fR, \fIdependencies\fR.\& Dependencies that \fIproject.\&json\fR lists for a
single target are part of the project too (\fBlist\fR, \fBverify\fR, \fBsync --frozen\fR).\&
.PP
Versions are chosen as in Go (minimum version selection): the highest of all
requested minimums, never newer.\& Versions that are not compatible are an
error, with the libraries on both sides named.\& Compatible means, as in Cargo,
the same major version, and below 1.\&0 the same minor (0.\&3.\&1 and 0.\&3.\&5, not 0.\&3
and 0.\&4: a 0.\&y release may break the one before); 0.\&0.\&z only matches itself.\& A cycle,
or a library requiring itself, is a warning (an error with \fB--strict\fR); each
library is installed once.\& Git sources other than github.\&com, codeberg.\&org and the
hosts of URLs given on the command line need \fB--allow-host\fR or an answer at the
prompt.\& More than 200 libraries are refused.\&
.PP
.SH PRIVATE REPOSITORIES
.PP
c3l runs \fBgit\fR for git libraries, so private repositories work with whatever gives
git access: an ssh key (\fIgit@github.\&com:me/lib\fR) or, for https URLs, a credential
helper (for GitHub: \fBgh auth setup-git\fR).\& git is never allowed to ask on the
terminal; when it fails, c3l shows what git said.\&
.PP
The same repository as \fIhttps://host/path\fR, \fIssh://git@host/path\fR and
\fIgit@host:path\fR counts as one source.\& Libraries should name their dependencies with
https URLs, which work for everyone; to fetch them over ssh yourself, let git
rewrite them:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
git config --global url\&."git@github\&.com:"\&.insteadOf https://github\&.com/
.fi
.RE
.PP
In CI, give git access to the other repositories: an ssh deploy key with the
rewrite above, or a token (in GitHub Actions a personal access token; the
built-in \fIGITHUB_TOKEN\fR reads only the repository being built):
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
git config --global url\&."https://x-access-token:${TOKEN}@github\&.com/"\&.insteadOf https://github\&.com/
.fi
.RE
.PP
.SH GIT SUBMODULES
.PP
A git library can also be kept as a git submodule at \fIlib/name.\&c3l\fR, for
example so that contributors without c3l get it with
\fBgit clone --recurse-submodules\fR.\& \fIc3l.\&lock\fR describes it like any git library
(URL, version, commit, content hash), and anyone who installs your library gets
it from that lockfile, as an archive.\& Projects whose \fI.\&gitmodules\fR names no
\fI.\&c3l\fR path are not affected.\&
.PP
\fBmigrate\fR adopts submodules the lockfile does not list: the URL from
\fI.\&gitmodules\fR (it must be absolute), the commit the repository records, a tag
at that commit as the version (else the branch \fI.\&gitmodules\fR follows, else the
commit), and what they require is installed.\& \fBsync\fR checks a submodule out, or
back to the recorded commit.\& \fBupdate\fR fetches the new commit into the
submodule, checks it out and stages it; c3l never commits.\& \fBverify\fR, \fBlist\fR
and \fBcheck\fR report a submodule that is \fInot-checked-out\fR, \fIedited\fR (local
changes), \fImoved\fR (another commit checked out), \fIlock-differs\fR (the repository
records another commit than \fIc3l.\&lock\fR; the message shows the \fBupdate\fR that
settles it either way) or \fIother-source\fR.\&
.PP
c3l never discards local changes or commits on no branch in a submodule, and
never replaces one with an archive or a link: \fBadd\fR and \fBprune\fR leave it alone,
and \fBremove\fR asks for \fBgit rm\fR first.\& The same holds for any git repository in
the library directory that holds work.\& Creating submodules, or converting
between a submodule and an archive, is left to git.\&
.PP
.SH LOCKFILE
.PP
Tab separated, one library per line, sorted by name:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
# c3l\&.lock v1
box2d	registry	https://www\&.c3pkg\&.eu	jecokef902/box2d	1\&.0\&.0	sha256:4945\&.\&.\&.	sha256:4945\&.\&.\&.	direct	-
hex	git	https://github\&.com/konimarti/hex\&.c3l	-	v0\&.1\&.1	commit:3fa9\&.\&.\&.	commit:3fa9\&.\&.\&.	direct	-
.fi
.RE
.PP
Columns: name, kind (\fIregistry\fR, \fIgit\fR or \fIpath\fR), origin, id, version, pin (checksum
or commit), what the installed file is checked against (the SHA-256 again for registry
libraries; for git \fIcontent:\fR and a SHA-256 over the names and contents of the
files in the archive, or the commit again in locks written by c3l 1.\&1), role
(\fIdirect\fR: added by you; \fIdep\fR: required by another library) and the comma
separated names the library requires (\fI-\fR for none).\&
.PP
The origin is where the library is fetched from: the registry base URL (no
trailing slash), the git repository URL, or the directory.\&
The id is \fInamespace/name\fR for a registry and \fI-\fR otherwise.\& Every line names its own
origin, so one project can mix registries.\& Library names stay unique: the same name
from two origins is an error (git URLs that differ only in a trailing \fI/\fR or \fI.\&git\fR, or
in case on github.\&com and codeberg.\&org, are the same origin).\& A file with another number
of columns is refused, and so is a line with an invalid name, checksum or commit: a
lockfile can come from someone else'\&s repository.\&
.PP
.SH SHELL COMPLETION
.PP
\fBc3l completion\fR prints a script that completes commands and options.\&
.PP
bash: add to \fI\(ti/.\&bashrc\fR, or save the script in \fI/etc/bash_completion.\&d/c3l\fR:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
source <(c3l completion bash)
.fi
.RE
.PP
zsh: add to \fI\(ti/.\&zshrc\fR, after \fBcompinit\fR:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
source <(c3l completion zsh)
.fi
.RE
.PP
fish:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
c3l completion fish > ~/\&.config/fish/completions/c3l\&.fish
.fi
.RE
.PP
.SH EXIT STATUS
.PP
0 on success, 1 when a command fails, 2 for a usage error (an unknown command or
option, a wrong number of arguments), 130 when interrupted (SIGINT or SIGTERM;
what the command changed so far is undone, a second signal stops at once).\&
.PP
.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.PP
\fIC3L_REGISTRY\fR
.RS 4
Registry base URL for new installs.\& Overridden by \fB--registry\fR.\&
Default: https://www.\&c3pkg.\&eu
.PP
.RE
\fIC3L_ALLOWED_HOSTS\fR
.RS 4
Comma or space separated git hosts that dependencies may fetch from, in addition to
github.\&com and codeberg.\&org.\&
.PP
.RE
\fIC3L_MAX_DEPS\fR
.RS 4
Largest number of transitive libraries one command may install.\& Default: 200.\&
.PP
.RE
\fIC3L_TOKEN\fR, \fIC3PKG_TOKEN\fR
.RS 4
API token for \fBpublish\fR, if no \fB--token-file\fR is given.\&
.PP
.RE
\fIC3L_REGISTRY_TYPE\fR
.RS 4
Same as \fB--registry-type\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fIC3C\fR
.RS 4
The c3c executable.\&
.PP
.RE
\fIC3L_LOCK\fR
.RS 4
Lockfile name.\& Default: \fIc3l.\&lock\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fIC3L_C3PKG_URL\fR, \fIC3L_C3LANG_URL\fR
.RS 4
Replace the URL of a default registry (a mirror, or tests).\&
.PP
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBc3c\fR(1)
.PP
